<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Getting an ID in Franklin County: the one page version</title>
<style>
{{ css }}

/* This sheet exists to be handed out on paper, so paper comes first. */
body { font-size: 11pt; padding: 0; }
.sheet {
  max-width: 7.1in;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: .35in;
}
.sheet h1 { font-size: 17pt; margin: 0 0 .1in; }
.sheet h2 { font-size: 12pt; margin: .16in 0 .04in; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
.sheet p, .sheet li { margin: .04in 0; font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 1.35; }
.sheet ul, .sheet ol { padding-left: .22in; margin: .04in 0; }
.cols { display: flex; gap: .3in; }
.cols > div { flex: 1; }
.tag { font-size: 9.5pt; color: var(--quiet); }
.draft {
  border: 2px solid var(--stop);
  color: var(--stop);
  padding: .06in .1in;
  margin: .08in 0;
  font-size: 10pt;
}
@page { size: letter portrait; margin: .4in; }
@media print {
  .sheet { padding: 0; max-width: none; }
  .noprint { display: none; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="sheet">

<h1>Getting an ID in Franklin County</h1>
<p class="tag">
  For people with no fixed address. Full guide, with your own list of steps:
  <b>{{ site_url }}</b>
</p>

{% if draft %}
<div class="draft">
  <b>Draft.</b> {{ unconfirmed }} of {{ fact_count }} facts still need a phone
  call. Do not hand this out until that is done.
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>The order that works</h2>
<ol>
  {% for step in sheet_steps %}
  <li><b>{{ step.title }}.</b> {{ step.first_line }}</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ol>
<p class="tag">
  Not every step applies to everyone. The full guide asks seven questions and
  gives a person only the steps they need.
</p>

<div class="cols">
<div>
<h2>Papers the BMV takes for an address</h2>
<ul>
  {% for doc in address_documents %}<li>{{ doc.plain_name }}</li>{% endfor %}
</ul>
<p class="tag">
  A shelter letter is <b>not</b> on the BMV list, and a friend cannot sign for you.
  Get one of the papers above mailed to you instead.
</p>
</div>
<div>
<h2>What to say at the counter</h2>
<ul>
  {% for step in key_steps %}
  <li><b>{{ step.short }}:</b> &ldquo;{{ step.what_to_say }}&rdquo;</li>
  {% endfor %}
</ul>
</div>
</div>

<h2>Where to go</h2>
{% for place in places %}
<p>
  <b>{{ place.name }}</b> &mdash; {{ place.address }}. {{ place.phone }}.
  {{ place.hours }}
</p>
{% endfor %}

<h2>If you get turned away</h2>
<p>
  Ask which paper was missing. Write down the date, the office, and who you
  spoke to. Then try a different office. Offices do not all work the same way,
  and that note is what lets a case manager push back.
</p>

<p class="tag">
  Not legal advice. Fees and hours change without notice, so call first.
  Facts last checked {{ newest_check }}. Oldest fact on this sheet: {{ oldest_check }}.
  Printed from {{ site_url }}. Built {{ build_date }}.
</p>

</main>
</body>
</html>
